; DescribedFilms.inix -- how this database opens, and how its tables are heard.
;
; ABOUT 10,000 ENGLISH MOVIES WITH AUDIO DESCRIPTION, from the Film and Series Title Directory of the American Council
; of the Blind's Audio Description Project (adp.acb.org): every movie it lists as available in the United States with
; English description, documentaries included and series left out. Each comes with its year, rating and genres, and
; the services that carry it.
;
; FIND ONE. The row speaks title, year and services: what it is, and where to watch it. Filter Records (Control+F) on
; services finds every film on one service, and on genres every documentary, comedy or western; F4 offers the values.
; Control+Shift+U opens the film's IMDb page.
;
; WATCH ONE. Alt+Right goes to the film's offers: one row a service, with its terms (buy, rent, free with Prime, a
; channel subscription) and its voice, which says "synthetic" when ADP marks the description as text-to-speech.
; Control+Shift+U on an offer opens the film on that service. Free-To-Watch lists the films free with a subscription
; or ads; Documentaries and Newest do what they say; Services-Count counts the films each service carries. The
; watch_list report writes up the marked films, to keep or print. Three come marked, to show how.
;
; scripts\makeDescribedFilms in DbDo's development folder rebuilds this file from the directory; the build runs it
; when the database is missing.
;
; Look is each table's default columns and prime its default order (5 November 2026); a table's saved columns, order
; and filter are written here only when a person chooses them.
; [Database] decides which table the window starts on. [Table:<name>] decides which fields the row speaks, in what
; order, and how the rows are sorted. DbDo writes these keys back whenever you change the columns, the sort or the
; filter.

[Database]

InitialTable = films

[Table:films]

; SelectFields, 19 November 2026: the services follow the title and year, since where to watch it is the question.
SelectFields = title, year, services

[Table:offers]

; SelectFields, 19 November 2026: the film first, which look leaves out because it is a link; DbDo says its title and year.
SelectFields = film_id, service, terms, voice

[Table:defs]


[Table:maps]
